    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We see ads every day, over 2000 of them. But… Can you even remember the last ad you saw? \n\nWhether it's on the internet, before a movie, on a shopping bag, in a rap song, or a product sitting on the set of a TV show, ads are everywhere. It's easy for people to say \"it’s okay, they're just ads\" because, at worst, people think that ads feel like a nuisance or interruption. They’re not an interruption. They are controlling you. Marketers use strategies such as \"reputation management\", \"Search engine Optimization\", \"Brand Affiliation\" and \"Inbound Marketing\" to make you buy things that you don't necessarily even want to buy. Learn more in this podcast!",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Leimgruber, Jesse (2014). Motion: The Force of Advertising. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/kc052dn5661",
